{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #251: declared status 'open'. Formalized: yes. Is\\[\\sum \\frac{p_n}{2^n}\\]irrational? (Here $p_n$ is the $n$th prime.) Current best: Erd\\H{o}s \\cite{Er58b} proved that $\\sum \\frac{p_n^k}{n!}$ is irrational for every $k\\geq 1$. In \\cite{Er88c} he further conjectures that $\\sum \\frac{p_n^k}{2^n}$ is irrational for every $k$, and that if $g_n\\geq 2$ and $g_n=o(p_n)$ then\\[\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\frac{p_n}{g_1\\cdots g_n}\\]is irrational. Prize: no. OEIS: A098990. Tags: irrationality, number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_fc24a67080e16b5b6575f7e393015834db1d87b54ff0128e35bbac776757c7ec","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:251","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_7ce74272755c55f9","object_root":"sha256:69d742aedef76b2d13a20d2cd928c0787ac4d37c6ab12adadc258fb3f7d42c9d","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:251"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record.v1"}